From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: widen license-files to cover re2 and abseil-cpp

`license-files = ["LICENSE"]` is an explicit PEP 639 list, so it has no
default glob behind it. On riscv64, the manylinux image has no EPEL
`re2-devel` to link against (gotcha 51), so the wheel instead builds
and statically links abseil-cpp (Apache-2.0) and re2 (BSD-3-Clause)
from source, with their upstream LICENSE files copied next to this
one as LICENSE.re2 and LICENSE.abseil-cpp. Widening the glob to
`LICENSE*` picks both up in dist-info/licenses without changing what a
clean checkout's sdist ships (still just LICENSE).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-only build detail; upstream's own CI links a system re2-devel package, never ships these extra notices]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 readme = { file = "README.rst", content-type = "text/x-rst" }
 requires-python = ">=3.10"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
-license-files = ["LICENSE"]
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 dynamic = ["version"]
 classifiers = [
     "Programming Language :: Cython",
-- 
2.43.0
